# Foundry
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
# contracts/lib/ is NOT ignored. forge-std is vendored there as plain files —
# no submodule, no .gitmodules — so ignoring it meant every clone of this repo
# failed to compile: "import {Test} from "forge-std/Test.sol"" resolves to
# nothing, and `forge test` is the command the submission tells a judge to run.
# 68 files, 1.3 MB, MIT.

# Data / artifacts
data/
*.parquet
scripts/_out/
.env
# A BACKUP OF .env IS STILL .env. `.env` on its own is an exact match, so
# `.env.bak-20261106T115437Z` — 48 assignments including three private keys and
# the Circle entity secret — sat untracked but VISIBLE to git in a public repo,
# one `git add -A` away from being published. Four sessions share this tree.
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store

# Competitive/ideation material that must never reach a PUBLIC repo.
# ETHGlobal_Online.md names prize targets, a designated-alternate contingency,
# a dropped-sponsor list and a counter-strategy to the continuity-scoring rule.
# It was nearly committed once; the entry is the guard, not the reminder.
ETHGlobal_Online.md
# Tameion (Canteen x Circle x Arc, Sep 27 - Oct 10 2026): the operator plan names
# a prior competition loss in one line, maps the build onto the judging weights,
# targets a ~120-developer community by name for outreach, and plans to ask rival
# teams in the cohort to route their spend through us because "judges notice it".
# The board carries the same traction tiers. Same rule as above: strategy for an
# ACTIVE, invite-only competition does not go in a public repo. The submission
# itself is public; the plan to win it is not.
Tameion_MachineTCA_Operator_Plan.md
Agoranomos_Tameion_Board.excalidraw
# The recording script for the submission video. The VIDEO is public; this is
# the sheet behind it, and its last section maps each beat onto the judging
# weights and says which beat to sacrifice if the cut runs long. Same rule as
# the plan above. Everything factual in it is already public in
# docs/WALKTHROUGH.md and docs/TAMEION.md.
Tameion_Video_Script.md
# The private implementation record: the same competition framing plus the
# unshipped items and the blocked list. docs/TAMEION.md is the public one.
TAMEION_IMPLEMENTATION.md
# Orphan scratch canvas. scripts/gen_architecture.py writes the TRACKED
# acr_architecture.excalidraw; nothing reads this one.
ACR_MachineTCA_Architecture_FULL.excalidraw
# The working register: ground state, market sizing, competitor analysis and a
# named outreach target list. Same rule as the entries above — the submission is
# public, the plan behind it is not. It also carries the defect register, which
# is honest internal engineering and not a thing to hand a reviewer out of
# context.
ACR_REGISTER.md

# Float's planning docs. They are the build plan for a hackathon entry, so they
# carry prize targeting, kill-gate decisions, demo stagecraft and the lines we
# plan to answer judges with. The product belongs in the repo; the strategy for
# winning with it does not — a judge clones this. What ships publicly is
# float/README.md and the continuity disclosure.
ACR_Float.md
ACR_float_flow_e2e.md
ACR_Float_Execution_Flows_1.excalidraw

# The fundraise set: the pitch, roadmap and business plan for the pre-seed round.
# Same rule as every entry above: the product is public, the round is not. It is
# also the one place the index demotion is argued in full, and that argument
# belongs in a conversation, not in a repo a stranger clones.
docs/fundraise/

# aomi-build writes local deploy state here; .aomi/config.json is committed.
.aomi/deployment.json
